From: Project SunUEFI <sunuefi@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/native: treat empty gamma as bypass before resampling

DisplayConfig SetCrtcGamma accepts three empty arrays, and GetCrtcGamma
returns these arrays when the KMS gamma LUT is unset. The CRTC cache copies
that request into a non-NULL, zero-sized MetaGammaLut. Resampling it to the
hardware LUT size divides by zero and reads sample -1 from its NULL arrays.

Keep the existing NULL bypass representation in the KMS color update for a
zero-sized LUT. The atomic backend then writes GAMMA_LUT=0. Non-empty LUTs
continue through the existing resampling path without changed sample data.

Applies to upstream Mutter 48.7. The current Debian 13 root uses source
mutter 48.7-0+deb13u1 (libmutter-16-0), with gnome-shell 48.7-0+deb13u2.
This is a source patch only; no patched package or device restore has yet
been built or verified.

Origin: https://github.com/GNOME/mutter/blob/48.7/src/backends/native/meta-kms-update.c
Forwarded: no
---
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-update.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-update.c
@@ -561,7 +561,8 @@
 
   g_assert (meta_kms_crtc_get_device (crtc) == update->device);
 
-  if (gamma)
+  /* A zero-sized LUT represents bypass and has no samples to resample. */
+  if (gamma && gamma->size > 0)
     gamma_update = meta_gamma_lut_copy_to_size (gamma, crtc_state->gamma.size);
 
   color_update = ensure_color_update (update, crtc);
